---
// Discoveries (#/discoveries): the tricks of the trade, one table. A trick is what a model can do,
// judged from outside by its bets (thorp/dash/tricks.py KNOWN_TRICKS; the ones Thorp measures are in
// fleet.TRICKS). A row opens the trick (#/discoveries/<trick>): the stars needed to learn it (the
// mechanisms inside, thorp/dash/heads.py), the size the field learns it at, and how Thorp is
// tracking, class by class, toward learning it at a smaller class. The star chart and the traits
// are one link away (#/discoveries/stars, #/discoveries/traits).
---
<div class="section" id="discoveries">

  <!-- ============================== the tricks of the trade -->
  <div class="dview" data-dview="index">
    <h1>Tricks of the trade</h1>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>The route to quantum physics <span class="note">seven waypoints, each resting on the one before; a waypoint's gate tricks (◆) are the ones a ship must perform before it moves on</span></h2>
      <div class="route" id="trickroute"></div>
    </section>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>The discovery chains <span class="note">the bettor's four tests (the Origin, energy, Mendeleev's gaps, the eternal return), each reached in six rungs, one per class, keel to bettor; the last row says what a model at each rung is, according to the four. Every class is scored on every rung; each cell is every class's best lift and best share of pairs right; ✓ is performed under the share rule (lift at 0.1 and two pairs in three right, at the same reading), ▲ passed below its class, ⚠ passed below its class while a bigger class fails it, so the pairs want auditing; Qwen3 0.6B for scale. Under each chain's name, its grade: graded when it gets harder at every rung across all the models read (no model passes a rung it fails below, fewer pass each rung, every rung reached)</span></h2>
      <div class="handtools"><label><input type="checkbox" id="chainrefidx"> show the reference ladder <span class="note">(Pythia 14m to 410m and Qwen3 0.6B to 4B, read on the same pairs)</span></label></div>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="chaintable" data-nosort><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>The tricks <span class="note">a trick is what a model can do, judged from outside by its bets; open one for the stars that do it and Thorp's progress, class by class. "The field shows it at" is the size band (one order of magnitude, in parameters) where the trick is documented in standard models, not a proven smallest size; hover a band for the detail. "Thorp's goal class" is the class of ship expected to reach it, about an order of magnitude smaller than the field where the depth it needs allows; ◆ marks a gate, performed before a ship moves on to the next waypoint</span></h2>
      <div class="handtools"><span class="note">waypoint</span><select id="trickfamily"><option value="">all</option></select><span class="note">the field shows it at</span><select id="trickband"><option value="">any size</option></select><span class="note" id="trickcount"></span></div>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="tricktable" class="clickable"><thead><tr><th>waypoint</th><th>trick</th><th>what it does</th><th>the field shows it at</th><th>how sure</th><th>stars needed</th><th>Thorp so far</th><th>Thorp's goal class</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
      <p class="note mt">Also: <a href="#/discoveries/stars">every kind of head (the star chart)</a> · <a href="#/discoveries/traits">traits</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== one trick -->
  <div class="dview" data-dview="trick">
    <h1><a href="#/discoveries" class="back">← discoveries</a> <span id="tricktitle"></span> <span id="trickstate"></span> <span class="q" id="trickdoes"></span></h1>
    <section class="panel"><div class="rungover" id="trickover"></div></section>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>The stars needed to learn it <span class="note">the mechanisms inside thought to do this trick, each with where it is expected and its state in Thorp</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="trickstars"><thead><tr><th>kind of head</th><th>what it does</th><th>rests on</th><th>expected from</th><th>first lit in</th><th>in Thorp</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>How Thorp is tracking, class by class <span class="note">each class of ship, how many of its sailings have been measured on this trick and how many performed it; the target is a tenth of the field's size</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="tricktrack"><thead><tr><th>class</th><th>parameters</th><th>against the field</th><th>sailings measured</th><th>performed</th><th>best</th><th>first performed</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <div class="row" id="trickcharts">
      <section class="panel" id="trickchartpanel">
        <h2>The trick, sailing by sailing <span class="note">its reading at every step, one line per sailing, coloured by class; the amber dotted line is the mark that counts as performed, the grey one the floor (an untrained ship), and labelled lines are outside models</span></h2>
        <div class="chart tall" id="trickchart"></div>
      </section>
      <section class="panel" id="trickpairpanel" hidden>
        <h2 id="trickpairtitle">Beside it</h2>
        <div class="chart tall" id="trickpairchart"></div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== one chain: a bettor's test told as a climb, keel to bettor (fleet.CHAINS) -->
  <div class="dview" data-dview="chain">
    <h1><a href="#/discoveries" class="back">← discoveries</a> <span id="chaintitle"></span> <span id="chainstrand"></span></h1>
    <section class="panel"><div class="rungover" id="chainover"></div></section>
    <div class="handtools"><label><input type="checkbox" id="chainrefpage"> show the reference ladder <span class="note">(Pythia 14m to 410m and Qwen3 0.6B to 4B beside each step's evidence)</span></label></div>
    <div id="chainsteps"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== the stars -->
  <div class="dview" data-dview="stars">
    <h1><a href="#/discoveries" class="back">← discoveries</a> The stars <span class="q">what inside does it? attention heads that do one recognisable job; a star is lit when one head reaches its threshold, and lit shared when the best layer's two strongest heads reach it together; some rest on others</span></h1>
    <div class="handtools"><button data-essay="nevermore">Read: what a Nevermore is</button></div>
    <div class="cards" id="starcards"></div>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>The star chart <span class="note">every kind of attention head described so far. Those Thorp measures carry their state from the ledger; the rest are charted but not yet measured, each with how Thorp could measure it. "Rests on" is the dependency its source reports; a blank means none reported. "Expected from" is the smallest class predicted to reach it (the floor is depth: one hop per layer), set beside the smallest class where a sailing has lit it</span></h2>
      <div class="handtools"><span class="note">family</span><select id="headfamily"><option value="">all</option></select><span class="note" id="headcount"></span></div>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="headtable"><thead><tr><th>kind of head</th><th>family</th><th>what it does</th><th>rests on</th><th>expected from</th><th>first lit in</th><th>in Thorp</th><th>first described</th><th>seen in</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== the traits -->
  <div class="dview" data-dview="traits">
    <h1><a href="#/discoveries" class="back">← discoveries</a> Traits <span class="q">can a ship's hidden state tell fiction, verse, first person or a language family apart on books it has never read; found at the threshold, learned when it also clears the floors</span></h1>
    <div class="handtools"><button data-essay="traits">Read: how traits are found</button></div>
    <section class="panel"><div class="scroll"><table id="traittable" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
  </div>
</div>
